From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:29:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The controller only has runtime PM ops, and a peripheral kept
runtime-active (the WCD9390 on the AYN Odin 3, held for jack detection)
keeps it active through s2idle, together with the LPASS macro clocks it
uses. Force the runtime suspend across system sleep, so jack detection
keeps working while awake but the ADSP can release LPASS in s2idle.

Only do this on buses with clock stop. Without it (the WSA881x speaker
bus on SM8250), the runtime resume resets the controller and loses the
ports of any stream still open, so leave those buses as they were.
---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index b288218f6..190fafc16 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -222,6 +222,7 @@ struct qcom_swrm_ctrl {
 	u32 slave_status;
 	u32 wr_fifo_depth;
 	bool clock_stop_not_supported;
+	bool sleep_suspended;
 };
 
 struct qcom_swrm_data {
@@ -1807,7 +1808,29 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int __maybe_unused swrm_suspend(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	ctrl->sleep_suspended = !ctrl->clock_stop_not_supported;
+	if (!ctrl->sleep_suspended)
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+}
+
+static int __maybe_unused swrm_resume(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	if (!ctrl->sleep_suspended)
+		return 0;
+
+	return pm_runtime_force_resume(dev);
+}
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops swrm_dev_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(swrm_suspend, swrm_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(swrm_runtime_suspend, swrm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
